@0    = ~"The yuan-ti stood there. The man was holding his trusted katana. He was ready for everything. He shall never give up: the heavens are on his side!"~
@1    = ~"The heart of the clearing was calm, but the tranquility was just about to turn into a battle. The yuan-ti warlord was on his way. He was there to kill the swordsman. For his life. For Shou Lung."~
@2    = ~I think I know this tale, my friend! It's a tale of a truly great battle. And a tale of a powerful sword.~
@3    = ~I think I know this tale, my friend! It's a tale of a truly great battle. And a tale of a powerful sword—Celestial Fury! The very same one we already have.~
@4    = ~This is a tale of a man from Shou Lung, and the love between him and an archon. Some would consider it heartbreaking. If you decide to learn from it, you'll need to pay 3,500 gold pieces. Then, you will take the place of the yuan-ti warlord and face the warrior.~
@5    = ~Yes. Let me see how determined that man truly was.~
@6    = ~No. I'll pass. At least for now.~
@7    = ~Of course. I truly hope you are ready to fight that monstrous fanatic. Now, close your eyes. Let the story take you.~
@8    = ~"The archon was called back to her deity, to Kwan Ying. On one hand, she understood Chin Yi's anger, as well as her grief. On the other hand, her archon's fury saddened her. In the end, Kwan Ying gave new shape to her trusted celestial: she let her rage become the scream of the Celestial Fury, a powerful sword, born from her beloved one's sword."~
@9    = ~Who shall learn from this tale? Who shall embrace the fury? Or shall you rather focus on the heavenly peace that was rejected once the storm came?~
@10   = ~I chose to see this as a story of wrath and revenge. I can understand where all that anger came from.~
@11   = ~I chose to see this as a story of heavenly love, so electric, and a rejection of peace that felt more like ignorance.~
@12   = ~And who shall learn from it? Who shall know the wrath?~
@13   = ~<PLAYER1>.~
@14   = ~<PLAYER2>.~
@15   = ~<PLAYER3>.~
@16   = ~<PLAYER4>.~
@17   = ~<PLAYER5>.~
@18   = ~<PLAYER6>.~
@19   = ~Who shall learn to understand that electrifying feeling you speak of?~
@20   = ~It shall be as you've decided. They shall understand the power of true fury.~
@21   = ~You've already faced the battle this book describes.~